{"id": "fh-0201", "domain": "blog database schema", "names": ["Users", "Posts", "Likes", "Comments", "Tags"], "text": "I'm drawing the database schema for our blog so the backend team can review it. Users connects to Posts, and Posts connects to Comments. Likes should connect to Posts too, with a dotted line. Tags is a small blue diamond, make it that way. Is Comments directly linked to Users? Move Tags below Posts. Make Users large. Which shape has the most connections? Label Posts as \"Articles\", since that's the name in the product. Rename Likes to Reactions. Duplicate Comments once, we need a second table. How many arrows are there in total? Undo the last rename if the team prefers Likes. Thanks, this looks much cleaner now.", "wires": [{"span": "Users connects to Posts, and Posts connects to Comments", "trigger": "connects to", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Users,Posts,Comments", "pairing": "chain"}}, {"span": "Likes should connect to Posts too, with a dotted line", "trigger": "connect", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Likes", "to": "Posts", "style": "dotted", "arrow": "none"}}, {"span": "Tags is a small blue diamond", "trigger": "is", "type": "fact", "args": {"target": "Tags", "shape": "diamond", "size": "small", "color": "blue"}}, {"span": "Is Comments directly linked to Users", "trigger": "directly linked to", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "connected", "target": "Comments", "anchor": "Users"}}, {"span": "Move Tags below Posts", "trigger": "Move", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Tags", "position": "below", "anchor": "Posts"}}, {"span": "Make Users large", "trigger": "Make", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "set", "target": "Users", "size": "large"}}, {"span": "Which shape has the most connections", "trigger": "most connections", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "extreme", "superlative": "mostConnected"}}, {"span": "Label Posts as \"Articles\"", "trigger": "Label", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "label", "target": "Posts", "label": "Articles"}}, {"span": "Rename Likes to Reactions", "trigger": "Rename", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "rename", "target": "Likes", "name": "Reactions"}}, {"span": "Duplicate Comments once", "trigger": "Duplicate", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "duplicate", "target": "Comments"}}, {"span": "How many arrows are there in total", "trigger": "How many arrows", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "count", "kind": "edge"}}, {"span": "Undo the last rename", "trigger": "Undo", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "undo"}}]}
{"id": "fh-0202", "domain": "scout campsite plan", "names": ["Tent1", "Tent2", "Fire", "Lake", "Parking"], "text": "We are planning the campsite layout for the scout trip and I want the tents to be clear. Tent1 and Tent2 face the Fire, so put them above it. Parking should be at the bottom left, the cars must stay away from the tents. Lake is to the right of the Fire. Connect Parking to Tent1 with a dashed line. Make Fire orange so the kids can find it. Which shape is the farthest from Parking? Is Tent2 near Fire? Arrange the tents in a row. Rename Lake to Pond, the kids call it that. Put a small green circle named Tree near the Fire. Count how many things we have. Thanks, the scouts will love this!", "wires": [{"span": "put them above it", "trigger": "put", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Tent1,Tent2", "position": "above", "anchor": "Fire"}}, {"span": "Parking should be at the bottom left", "trigger": "should be at", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Parking", "position": "bottomLeft"}}, {"span": "Lake is to the right of the Fire", "trigger": "is to the right of", "type": "fact", "args": {"target": "Lake", "position": "rightOf", "anchor": "Fire"}}, {"span": "Connect Parking to Tent1 with a dashed line", "trigger": "Connect", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Parking", "to": "Tent1", "style": "dashed", "arrow": "none"}}, {"span": "Make Fire orange", "trigger": "Make", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "set", "target": "Fire", "color": "orange"}}, {"span": "Which shape is the farthest from Parking", "trigger": "farthest from", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "nearest", "anchor": "Parking", "superlative": "farthest"}}, {"span": "Is Tent2 near Fire", "trigger": "Is Tent2 near", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "check", "target": "Tent2", "position": "near", "anchor": "Fire"}}, {"span": "Arrange the tents in a row", "trigger": "Arrange", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "arrange", "target": "Tent1,Tent2", "layout": "row"}}, {"span": "Rename Lake to Pond", "trigger": "Rename", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "rename", "target": "Lake", "name": "Pond"}}, {"span": "Put a small green circle named Tree near the Fire", "trigger": "Put", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "create", "shape": "circle", "size": "small", "color": "green", "name": "Tree", "position": "near", "anchor": "Fire"}}, {"span": "Count how many things we have", "trigger": "Count how many things", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "count"}}]}
{"id": "fh-0203", "domain": "school timetable for parents", "names": ["Math", "Science", "History", "Art", "Gym", "Lunch"], "text": "This is my timetable for the school year, I'm drawing it so the parents can understand the day. Math comes first, then Science, then History. Connect those in a chain. Art and Gym should be next to each other on the right. Lunch sits between History and Art, put it there. Make Lunch yellow because everyone loves lunch. Is Gym left of Art? Hmm, I think it's the other way round, so move Gym to the left of Art. Which shape is the leftmost? Describe the whole timetable for the school website. Show me all the yellow shapes. Rename Gym to PE, that's what the kids say. Undo the last move if the layout becomes confusing. Thanks, the principal is reviewing this on Monday.", "wires": [{"span": "Connect those in a chain", "trigger": "Connect", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Math,Science,History", "pairing": "chain"}}, {"span": "Lunch sits between History and Art, put it there", "trigger": "sits between", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Lunch", "position": "between", "anchor": "History,Art"}}, {"span": "Make Lunch yellow", "trigger": "Make", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "set", "target": "Lunch", "color": "yellow"}}, {"span": "Is Gym left of Art", "trigger": "left of", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "check", "target": "Gym", "position": "leftOf", "anchor": "Art"}}, {"span": "move Gym to the left of Art", "trigger": "move", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Gym", "position": "leftOf", "anchor": "Art"}}, {"span": "Which shape is the leftmost", "trigger": "leftmost", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "extreme", "superlative": "leftmost"}}, {"span": "Describe the whole timetable for the school website", "trigger": "Describe", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "describe"}}, {"span": "Show me all the yellow shapes", "trigger": "Show me all", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "list", "color": "yellow"}}, {"span": "Rename Gym to PE", "trigger": "Rename", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "rename", "target": "Gym", "name": "PE"}}, {"span": "Undo the last move", "trigger": "Undo", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "undo"}}]}
{"id": "fh-0204", "domain": "library sections", "names": ["Fiction", "Science", "Kids", "Desk"], "text": "Lay the sections out in a circle. Desk should be in the middle. Is Kids next to Desk? Make Fiction blue.", "wires": [{"span": "Lay the sections out in a circle", "trigger": "Lay the sections out", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "arrange", "target": "Fiction,Science,Kids,Desk", "layout": "circle"}}, {"span": "Desk should be in the middle", "trigger": "should be in", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Desk", "position": "center"}}, {"span": "Is Kids next to Desk", "trigger": "Is Kids next to", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "check", "target": "Kids", "position": "near", "anchor": "Desk"}}, {"span": "Make Fiction blue", "trigger": "Make", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "set", "target": "Fiction", "color": "blue"}}]}
